SCOPE (EU) 2026/188 OF THE COMMISSION
amending the Annex to the Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447 on emergency measures in relation to outbreaks of high-pharmacous bird flu in certain Member States
Having regard to Regulation (EU) 2016/429 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 9 March 2016 on animal transmission diseases and amending and repealing certain acts in the field of animal health (‘Animal Health Law’) ( 1 ), and in particular Article 259(1) thereof,
In order to ensure uniform conditions for the implementation of this Regulation, implementing powers should be conferred on the Commission.
Regulation (EU) 2016/429 establishes the legislative framework for the prevention and control of diseases which are inputable to animals or humans. HPAI under the definition of listed disease in that Regulation, and is subject to the disease prevention and control rules laid down therein. In addition, Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/687 ( 2 ) supplementing Regulation (EU) 2016/429 as regards rules on the prevention and control of certain listed diseases, including HPAI. In particular, Article 21 of that Delegated Regulation provides, in the case of an outbreak of disease of category A in an establishment, that the competent authority is to establish an immediate restricted zone comprising a protected zone, a surveillance zone, a surveillance zone, and if necessary, additional restricted zones around and surveillance zones.
The Commission’s Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447 ( 3) was adopted on the basis of Regulation (EU) 2016/429, and lays down emergency measures at Union level in relation to HPAI outbreaks.
In particular, Article 2, point (a), point (a), and Article 4, point (a) of the Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447, provides, respectively, for the inclusion of the areas listed as protected zones and surveillance and additional restricted zones in that Annex. Article 2, point (b), point (b), and Article 4, point (b), of the Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447 also provides that the measures to be applied in those protected zones, surveillance and additional restricted zones, in accordance with that Delegated Regulation, must also be maintained until the dates set out in the Annex to that Implementing Decision.
The Annex to the Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447 was last amended by Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2026/1796 ( 4 ) following an outbreak of HPAI in Poland in an establishment where birds were kept in captivity.
From the date of adoption of the Implementing Decision (EU) 2026/1796, the Netherlands has notified the Commission of an outbreak of HPAI in that Member State in an establishment where birds were kept in captivity, in the province of Zuid Holand.
In order to ensure uniform conditions for the implementation of this Regulation, implementing powers should be conferred on the Commission.
The Commission has examined the disease control measures taken by the Netherlands and is satisfied that, as regards the limits of the protected and surveillance zones established for the reported outbreak, they are quite long from the establishment where the HPAI outbreak is certified.
In order to prevent any unnecessarily unnecessary disturbance of trade within the Union, it is necessary to report rapidly at Union level, in cooperation with the Netherlands, on the protected and surveillance zones established by that Member State in accordance with Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/687.
In the Annex to the Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447, no area is currently listed as protected and surveillance zones for the Netherlands. Therefore, the areas concerned should be listed as protected and surveillance zones in the Netherlands, taking into account the limits of those zones established by the Netherlands, as well as the necessary duration of the measures to be applied in those zones, in accordance with Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/687.
The Annex to the Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447 should therefore be amended accordingly.
In view of the urgency of the economic situation in the Union as regards the dissemination of HPAI, it is important that the amendments to the Annex to the Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447 enter into force as soon as possible.
The Annex to the Implementing Decision (EU) 20233/2447 is replaced by the text set out in the Annex to this Decision.
This Decision is addressed to the Member States.
( 1 ) OJ L 84, 31.3.2016, p. 1 , ELI: http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/429/oj .
( 2 ) Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2020/687 of 17 December 2019 supplementing Regulation (EU) 2016/4229 of the European Parliament and of the Council as regards the prevention and control of rules on certain listed diseases (OJ L 174, 3.6.2020, p. 64, ELI: http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_del/2020/687/oj).
( 3 ) Commission Implementing Decision 2023/2447 of 24 October 2023 on emergency measures in relation to the outbreaks of high-pharmacists in certain Member States (OJ L 2023/2447, 30.10.2023, ELI: http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2023/2447/oj).
( 4 ) Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2026/1796 of 16 July 2026 amending the Annex to the Implementing Decision (EU) 2023/2447 on emergency measures in relation to the outbreaks of high-pacic poultry in certain Member States (OJ L 2026/1796, 20.7.2026, ELI: http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2026/1796/oj).
The Commission shall adopt implementing acts laying down the arrangements for the application of this Regulation.
